lesson: 235
title: Overs, holes, frames and halves
level: primary-3
stars: 1
explain: In cricket an over is 6 balls bowled by one bowler.
explain: The scoreboard shows overs and balls: 12.3 overs means 12 full overs and 3 balls of the next one.
explain: 12 overs and 3 balls: 12 × 6 + 3 = 72 + 3 = 75 balls.
vars: a=name n=3..15 k=2..5
let: m = n + 1
answer: n * 6 + k
exercise: In a cricket match, {a} has bowled {n} overs and {k} more balls. How many balls has {a.he} bowled?
exercise: The scoreboard shows that {n} overs and {k} balls have been bowled. How many balls is that?
exercise: How many balls have been bowled after {n} complete overs and {k} balls of the next over?
exercise: {a}'s team batted for {n} overs and {k} balls before they were all out. How many balls did they face?
exercise: In the school match, {a} bowls {n} overs, then {k} balls before it rains. How many balls does {a.he} bowl?
exercise: {n} overs n {k} balls gone. how many balls is that
exercise: bowled {n-1} overs, no wait {n} overs and {k} balls. how many balls
exercise: {a} been bowling all arvo, {n} overs and {k} balls, plus took 2 wickets but whatever. balls bowled?
exercise: my mate says {n} overs {k} balls is {n*10+k} balls lol. what is it really
exercise: cricket, {n}.{k} overs on the board. how many balls is that
test: What number of balls has been bowled when the scoreboard reads {n} overs and {k} balls?
test: {k} balls into the {m.ord} over, how many balls bowled so far
test: {a} faces every ball of {n} overs and then {k} more. Count the balls {a.he} faces.
test: scoreboard says {n}.{k} overs. balls?
test: The umpire counts {n} full overs and {k} balls. Find the number of balls.
test: The bowler has just bowled the {k.ord} ball of the {m.ord} over. How many balls have been bowled in the innings?
exam: Determine the aggregate number of deliveries bowled upon completion of {n.words} overs together with {k.words} further deliveries.
exam: It is given that the scorebook records {n} completed overs and {k} additional balls. Ascertain the total number of legitimate deliveries.
exam: Compute the number of balls delivered by {a}, whereas {a.he} is credited with {n} overs and {k} balls.
exam: Pursuant to the laws of cricket, state the number of fair deliveries comprised in an innings lasting {n} overs and {k} balls.
exercise: The match was stopped when the groundsman's dog "made a mess" on the pitch. By then {n} overs and {k} balls had been bowled. How many balls had been bowled?
exercise: umpire "needed a comfort break" at {n}.{k} overs, bloody hell, again. how many balls bowled
test: {a} admits {a.he} "misremembered" the score: when the match was called off, it was not {n+1} full overs but {n} overs and {k} balls. How many balls had been bowled?
